// otter-in-the-window-seat: an airliner built twenty times life, full of otters at their machines. The visitor is the
// signal: over the roof past an otter sat up beside the dome with a paw on an aerial, down the sun flank past a loose
// raft of sea otters on a cloud top and an otter that slides down the wing on its belly, in by a window that has a rim and no pane, up the aisle in one climb from its sitters' faces
// to a gallery above their caps and over the dusk rows while screens wake as its arcs of light pass them, and out through the glass of the one laptop an otter has turned to show us.
//
// DECLARED (design/ab/otter-in-the-window-seat.design.json, `declared`), in plain words:
// - DECLARED PACING: the pulses of three arcs travel the ROUTE ahead of the visitor by a law of the metres flown alone
//   (plan file, ARCS): pulse k is born at route metre 24 k and runs ahead at 2.2 times the eye's own metres until it
//   is 32.4 m in front. They overtake the eye, are never steered by the lens, and the lens can turn away from them. They
//   read ctx.flight.rate only to go out when the flight is hurried. Each comes in over 6 m flown and goes out over
//   its last 8; the one whose station reaches the mouth of the hero's row gap (born at m 432) goes out eased over
//   its station's last 13.2 m of route before that mouth (6 m flown), nought where it meets it. That strength is a
//   number 0..1; AN ARC IS NEVER SEEN PALE OR SEE-THROUGH BY IT (outside part, the arcs' vertex law): at every
//   strength the ribbon keeps its full colour and its one opacity, and the strength SHAPES it: the share of the arc
//   that stands is the strength raised to the power 0.6 (times its fit in the picture, see the read of the lens); its
//   width is that share of its full width (to a hair of 2.2 px, then nothing at or under a share of 0.06) and its sweep
//   opens from three tenths of its fan (whole from a share of 0.7: a drawn arc is a short thin arc at the least, never a dot). The light a pulse throws on seats and the ceiling's blue still go by strength.
// - KEYED TO THE METRES FLOWN, not to nearness and not to a clock: the wave (each seat's station is a number of
//   metres flown, fixed at build from the route's table and the arcs' law, the same on every visit and at every
//   pace); the arcs; the roof otter's head, lifted and coming round with the eye (route m 30 to 60: before and after
//   it turns by the clock); the ceiling's blue (a soft brightening on the two light bars, the ceiling beside them and
//   the aisle's carpet under them
//   where a pulse of three arcs stands and for 60 m the way it runs, its light thrown on before it: the very numbers of
//   the arcs' frames, the station's z and its heading, uniforms only); and the aims of three looks, which slide
//   with the eye's own place on the route (the look from the raft to the entered window: first the slider's way on
//   the wing, then a point of the ROW OF WINDOWS that runs down the row to the entered one as the eye comes in to
//   the skin; the look down the sun block's aisle seats from the bay to the wheel; and the look at the machines
//   ahead over the far block). Nothing else.
// - PLACED TO BE SEEN FROM THE WAY, for the whole flight, on every seed: the hero's machine is turned a quarter to
//   face the row gap the last leg flies, and its three arcs stand in the lid's plane; the sun block's row 0 keeps two
//   seats empty, AND SO DOES THE FAR BLOCK'S ROW 0 ACROSS THE AISLE (its aisle and middle seats, trays stowed: the
//   line comes down over them to the row gap, and a sitter there, awake or asleep, was seen from above and behind as
//   a brown lump cut by the picture's lower edge), AND THE AISLE SEATS OF ROW 1 IN BOTH BLOCKS ARE EMPTY TOO, trays
//   stowed (the sun block's, beside the one stood up: the line climbs the aisle right behind and above it, and the one
//   in headphones who sat there filled the picture's lower edge from behind; the far block's: from the line above it
//   was a head cut by the picture's lower left corner, a cup on the lower edge); three typists sit in the sun block's
//   front row; the named sitters sit beside the aisle and the climb or under the leg over the far block (THE ONE IN
//   HEADPHONES, the only one of the cabin, in the window seat of the far block's row 0, no part of it nearer the line
//   than 6 m, counted); the aisle seats of rows -1 to 5 are never empty (but those of rows 0 and 1 in both blocks,
//   kept empty by the plan); a lit bar runs along
//   the aisle's edge at the foot of every row of seats; the far block's rows 1 to 3 hold laptops in their middle and window
//   seats; the raft's tower stands outside the descent; the roof otter sits up beside the dome's aft end (the end nearest the line flown), turned
//   to the coming line, its paw on the second aerial; THE WINDOW CLOUD (plan, WINDOW_CLOUD: two sea otters afloat on a
//   small cloud top of its own with a belly under it, on every visit) stands in the open sky 160 m beyond the sun
//   wall, forward of the wing's swept leading edge and 5 m under the wing's own face at that span: from no place of
//   the flown line outside does a sight line through it or its otters go on to meet the wing or the hull (it is seen
//   against sky and cloud sea, never lying on the metal; counted on the true triangles), and between route m 470 and
//   m 491, about the last leg's start, an otter's head stands in the hero's own window, about 200 m off (counted; small there, by that
//   distance); the dome's three arcs standing in an upright plane turned between the
//   hull's axis and the coming line; the crew otter sits straight ahead of the entered window. THE ONE STOOD UP: the
//   sun block's row 1 MIDDLE seat holds an otter that STANDS ON ITS HIND LEGS on its own cushion, an otter of a
//   sitter's own proportions (no part of neck, trunk or arm drawn out beyond 1.1 of a sitter's: counted), turned to
//   the aisle, HOLDING NOTHING: both its paws hang before its belly as an otter stood upright holds them, nothing
//   above its shoulders (the cap of the seat before it is out of an otter's reach, and its paw is no longer hooked
//   over its own seat's cap), its tail laid in a round where it sat; it looks down the aisle toward the coming line and round
//   to the aisle abeam by the world's clock (plan, UP and upAt: no part of it nearer the flown line than 7 m,
//   counted). From the aisle its head comes up over the caps of rows -1 and 0 as the eye climbs (it is as high as its
//   legs make it, and no higher); the aisle seat beside it is empty, so that from the aisle nothing stands before it. NOTHING LIES ON A SEAT'S
//   CUSHION AND NOTHING HANGS OVER A CAP OR AN ARMREST anywhere in the cabin (no blanket, no hung headphones).
//   FACES AT THE GLASS (plan, GLASS): the window seats of the sun block's rows 1 and 2 hold otters bent to their
//   windows, a paw on the reveal, and one more stands on its hind legs on a plain case hard by the wall at the bay's
//   own window (unit -2), a paw on the rim, the same on every visit. THE FRONT ROW'S LIDS lie back flatter (plan, D.LID_FRONT) so that its three faces stand clear above
//   them from the bay; every lid's back but the hero's carries one plain sticker (a small picture on a paper label: a fish over a wave, kelp or a sailing boat, by its sitter's own
//   phase draw: no draw of its own).
//   THE GALLEY'S MOUTH: each partition's doorway opens on a lit recess with a counter, the curtain drawn back in two
//   gathered halves. THE READING LAMPS of the dusk end (main part, lampLit: from the dusk row on, two seats in
//   three, by place) throw a warm pool on the fur and on what lies under them: the tray and the machine's deck on it,
//   or the cushion of an empty seat (DUSK.pool); no light of the rig. THE DUSK END is a warm violet (DUSK: the six
//   lamps of the cove over rows 3 to 8), not a blue one.
//   THE LIGHT THAT FALLS ON SEATS (main part, makeGlow, one additive draw): every lit screen's light on the front of
//   its own seat's back (in the dusk rows DUSK.seat times as strong, by the seat's row), and the blue of the hero's three standing arcs on the fronts of the three seat backs of its
//   row, the hero's own and the two empty ones (plan, HERO.ARCS.LIGHT), each by its own clock. THE LAST TWO SEATS of
//   the wave's order (plan, WAVE.AWAKE) are dealt awake from the start of the cabin: no seat begins to wake under a
//   last pulse weaker than a half (counted).
//   The look at the roof otter (aimed at its chest, 3 m under its head) ends at a place of the roof (its head's x + 5 m) and a look at the dome under its
//   three arcs takes over there (the animal, 8 m beside the line, leaves by the frame's side). THE RAFT'S LOOK holds
//   the raft's middle from the roof's edge until the eye has come down past the raft, by the eye's own place; the
//   dome's three arcs are small enough to stand whole from the line abeam (plan, DOME.ARCS_R). BY PLACE in the
//   outside part: the arcs are not drawn inside the hull's own space; in a zone of the sun flank before the entered
//   window they are lifted over the window line; no wisp is drawn in the roof's clear air between the route's first
//   point and the crown group, nor in the lane of air outside the hero's own window through which the last leg's
//   first metres see the cloud of two (in plan 50 m out from the skin, from 4.4 m forward of that window's middle
//   to 9 m aft of it; a streak goes out over 8 m as it comes to it); the flank carries three doors a side, and every window's rim is warm with the look's
//   cabin glow. THE FUR'S FLOOR (main part): by the place alone no coat is seen under a quarter of its lit
//   colour, inside and outside, the same at every metre and from every side. TWO PLACES OF SOFT LIGHT in the fur's own law (plan,
//   HERO.FILL and UP.FILL: a place and a reach, no light of the scene) stand at the hero and at the one stood up,
//   whose seen sides are their shaded ones (it rises and falls a sixth in slow bands that drift over the coat by
//   the world's clock, as cloud passes the windows); the hero's own window throws no shaft of haze (its box is left out of
//   the kit's row), so that the hero is seen through clear air; AND EVERY OTHER WINDOW'S SHAFT BEGINS 11.4 m IN FROM
//   THE SUN WALL (the armrest between the window seat and the middle seat; world, SHAFT_X), so that an otter at the
//   glass is not washed pale by the root of its own window's beam. All of it the same at every metre and on every seed.
// - ON THE WORLD'S CLOCK: all idle life (waiting habits, paws, glances, nods, breath, whiskers, drinks, curtains, the
//   brightening that runs up every three arcs (on the glass, in the light they throw on seats and in the ceiling's
//   blue), pictures on screens and their light stirring on the seat behind, the craning of an otter stood up inside
//   (its whole body bobs on its legs and its trunk sways), the swell under the floating otters, their heads
//   lifting toward the flown line, one grooming, one tapping its shell, the hero's head going between the aisle and
//   its own machine's glass, the roof otter's head, the slider's round down the wing and back (20 s, no jump; its
//   drawn shade goes with it), coats in the wind, the cloud
//   sea, the wisps over the roof and their shade sliding along the skin, the dapple, motes).
// - READ OF THE LENS, for the thin-line law and for media only; never to place, hide or fade a body (the one vertex
//   law of a body it touches is a whisker's width), never for a look, a seed or a place: the cabin light's update reads the camera's field of view and the drawing buffer's
//   height into ONE number, the angle one pixel covers (uPix, main part, makeCabinLight). By it and by the true
//   distance to the lens a whisker is widened to a floor of a pixel and a half (as if no further off than 90 m; the
//   count takes that widening off every animal's figure) and the arcs' ribbons to a floor of 2.2 px laid, 1.9 drawn, either hand (outside part).
//   A billow's puff softens its edge by its size in the picture (the projection's scale, in its vertex law). The
//   lens's PLACE is read to shade (gloss, rim, the thin fog), to turn ribbons and puffs to face it and to thin a
//   medium near it: the wisps melt away between 46 and 10 m from the lens. THE ARCS ARE NEVER FADED BY IT: an arc's
//   ribbon NARROWS, at full colour and its one opacity, to a hair and then nothing: an outdoor arc's width between
//   16 and 6 m from the lens (and over the 1.25 m outside the hull's skin, inside which it is cut); a whole arc's
//   width and sweep (it closes to three tenths of its fan) between 2.9 and 2.1 of its radii from the lens to its middle (gone at about 2.2)
//   (nearer than that it cannot stand whole in the picture); an indoor sign's width between 2.5 and 0.6 m. The same
//   law at every metre flown, in every window's shape.
// - THE STORY THE WAVE TELLS: only seats within 20 m of where the signal ran wake; the sun block's window side and
//   the far dusk rows wait all flight. Meant.
// - NOTHING AT THE WAY OUT changes by the metres still to fly: the hero has no station, its pose, its machine and its
//   three arcs are the same at every metre; no seat takes a station from the last leg; no pulse enters the row gap.
//   The one change there is the engine's own reveal of the next world in its opening.
// - WHAT A SEED DEALS: the look of the sky (three, all with a low sun on the side of x = 0) and where the far cloud
//   towers stand (stream 'otter-look:' + seed); who sits in every seat that is not named or ruled, at which machine,
//   with which picture, drink, tint, size and waiting habit (stream 'otter-cast:' + seed; every seat's dice are drawn
//   before any test). The engine's own ctx.rng is handed to the kit's makers of the sky, the cloud sea, the towers and
//   the window light's motes, and to nothing of this world's own. A seed never touches the route, the entered window, the hero's row, the far block's row 0, the aisle seats of row 1, a named sitter, the
//   outside groups, the wave's law or the arcs' law. RULED OR LEFT OUT, THEIR DICE STILL DRAWN: the far block's
//   six laptops (rows 1 to 3, seats 0 and 1: always taken, always laptops); the far block's row 2 aisle seat (never
//   a laptop: a tumbler on the aisle end of its tray); the aisle seats of rows -1 to 5 (never empty, but those of
//   rows 0 and 1); every other sitter of rows 6 to 8 when
//   ctx.quality.detail is under 0.7. ctx.vary.rare stages one more sea otter afloat on a small cloud of its own
//   beyond the far windows; ctx.vary.density makes fewer seats empty; ctx.vary.mood warms or cools the cove.
// - A FIXED COAT: every build's tufts are scattered by ctx.core.makeRng(ctx.core.hashSeed('otter-coat')): the same
//   coat on every visit, by intent.
// - DEPARTURES FROM THE GUIDE: 57 s (guide 35 to 50); 7.2 to 7.3 m/s in the cabin, 6.2 to 6.3 round the wheel (guide 10 to 30: a room at twenty
//   times life is flown slowly); the last straight is 39 m on one heading with 14.5 m level (guide about 60 m); the
//   exit is in view for the last 67 m only, an eighth of the flight (guide the last third); the hours 'day' and
//   'night' are not honoured (a low-sun world: 'golden' asks for GOLD, 'dawn' for ROSE).
//
// Every number two files need lives in ../parts/otter-in-the-window-seat-plan.js (no import; the count reads it too).
// Places are metres of cabin space (the sun wall at x = 0, seats to +x, row k at z = 15.6 k) or metres of route.
import * as THREE from 'three';
import * as INT from '../kit/interior.js';
import { makePath } from '../kit/core.js';
import { makeSky, makeCloudFieldAsync } from '../kit/sky.js';
import * as P from '../parts/otter-in-the-window-seat-plan.js';
import * as M from '../parts/otter-in-the-window-seat.js';
import * as O from '../parts/otter-in-the-window-seat-outside.js';

const PI = Math.PI, D = P.D;
const mixHex = (a, b, t) => new THREE.Color(a).lerp(new THREE.Color(b), t);

// THE THREE LOOKS (dealt by the first draw of 'otter-look'; the sun's height is the plan's): what the kit sky, the
// cabin's rig, the fur's own light and the outside part are handed for each. All three keep the sun's strength in
// the cabin moderate, so that a pale chest in a window's sun holds its shape; and all three keep the rig's own
// ambient LOW and the windows' sky fill high, so that the rows whose blinds are up stand in the gold and rows 3 to 8
// (blinds down: no window row is handed to the rig there) stand in a violet dusk under the cove's lamps.
const LOOKS = {
  GOLD: {
    sky: { preset: 'goldenHour', zenith: '#1c3888', mid: '#5f7cc8', horizon: '#f0b266', horizonPow: 5.2, sunIntensity: 12, clouds: { coverage: 0.22 }, clouds2: { opacity: 0.3 } },
    fog: 0.00022, sun: '#ffbf74', sunI: 8.4, ambient: 1.0, ambSky: '#aab2e2', ambGround: '#8f7a78', bounceColor: '#b98a58', bounce: 3.4,
    win: ['#ffd6a0', 13], far: ['#b4c4f0', 6.5], out: { sky: '#a9c0f2', skyIntensity: 3.4, ground: '#f0c79a', groundIntensity: 1.7, sun: 0.5 },
    cove: ['#5f7ee0', '#8a86dc', 7.0], glow: ['#ffb070', 15], shaftGain: 0.4, fill: 2.0, sea: { silver: 1.6 },
    E: { sun: '#ffc27e', sky: '#9fb4e4', ground: '#e9c49c' },
    post: { exposure: 1.0, bloom: { strength: 0.34, radius: 0.6, threshold: 1.1 }, grade: { saturation: 1.1, contrast: 1.06, vignette: 0.26, grain: 0.02 } },
  },
  ROSE: {
    sky: { preset: 'dawn', zenith: '#2a2f7c', mid: '#8a76b8', horizon: '#f0a898', scatterColor: '#ff9a7a', scatter: 0.75, sunColor: '#ffb48c', sunIntensity: 12, stars: 0, clouds: { coverage: 0.2 }, clouds2: { opacity: 0.34 } },
    fog: 0.00024, sun: '#ffa66e', sunI: 8, ambient: 1.05, ambSky: '#b0a8dc', ambGround: '#8c7078', bounceColor: '#b47e66', bounce: 3.4,
    win: ['#ffc4a4', 12], far: ['#b0b0ea', 6.2], out: { sky: '#b0b2ee', skyIntensity: 3.2, ground: '#f0b8a0', groundIntensity: 1.7, sun: 0.5 },
    cove: ['#6a78de', '#9884d8', 7.6], glow: ['#ff9c78', 15], shaftGain: 0.42, fill: 2.0, sea: { silver: 1.5 },
    E: { sun: '#ffb08a', sky: '#a3a4e0', ground: '#e6b4a0' },
    post: { exposure: 1.0, bloom: { strength: 0.34, radius: 0.6, threshold: 1.1 }, grade: { saturation: 1.06, contrast: 1.04, vignette: 0.26, grain: 0.02 } },
  },
  AFTERGLOW: {
    sky: { preset: 'sunset', zenith: '#101c58', mid: '#58408c', horizon: '#d8747a', sunElevation: 5, sunIntensity: 12, stars: 0, clouds: { coverage: 0.18 }, clouds2: { opacity: 0.3 } },
    fog: 0.00026, sun: '#ff9a5c', sunI: 7.6, ambient: 1.1, ambSky: '#a8a4de', ambGround: '#84687c', bounceColor: '#a8705e', bounce: 3.2,
    // (out: the fur under the open sky takes the warm of this look's orange cloud sea from below and a rose sky from
    // above, so that a sea otter's pale head reads buff on the cloud top and not grey)
    win: ['#ffb088', 11], far: ['#9a9ee6', 6], out: { sky: '#c4a8cc', skyIntensity: 2.8, ground: '#f2a878', groundIntensity: 2.0, sun: 0.6 },
    cove: ['#7280e0', '#a088d8', 8.4], glow: ['#ff8a60', 14], shaftGain: 0.46, fill: 2.0, sea: { silver: 1.7 },
    E: { sun: '#ff9460', sky: '#8a88cc', ground: '#b48a98' },
    post: { exposure: 1.04, bloom: { strength: 0.36, radius: 0.6, threshold: 1.1 }, grade: { saturation: 1.06, contrast: 1.04, vignette: 0.28, grain: 0.02 } },
  },
};

// THE DUSK END'S OWN LIGHT (rows 3 to 8, by place: the cove's lamps stand over those rows only). The room there is held
// low and A WARM VIOLET (each lamp at `lamp` of the look's cove strength, its colour `mix` of the way to `deep`; it was a
// deep blue, and the room read as cold navy with near-black seats), while the fur keeps the look's own soft cove; and
// every glass lights its sitter's face and chest strongly (`glowWait` for a waiting glass, the blue of its three arcs;
// `glow` for one that has woken) and the front of its own seat's back (`seat`: the dusk rows' share of the part's
// GLOW.SEAT, by the seat's row): in the dusk the faces are the lamps. `pool`: the strength of a reading lamp's warm pool
// where it lies on a tray or on an empty seat's cushion (by place: the part's lampLit).
const DUSK = { lamp: 0.85, deep: '#8452c0', mix: 0.7, glow: 4.2, glowWait: 7.0, seat: 2.0, pool: 1.0 };
// WHERE THE WINDOWS' SHAFTS OF HAZE BEGIN (a place: metres in from the sun wall): the middle of the armrest between the
// window seat and the middle seat, x 11.4. See step 11.
const SHAFT_X = D.SEAT_X0 + D.ARM_W + D.SEAT_W + D.ARM_W / 2;

// the route metre at which the eye first comes level with a place, between two route metres: the first crossing of
// one coordinate (axis 0 x, 1 y, 2 z) through a value, read from the ONE TABLE of the route (never a typed share)
function levelMetre(T, axis, value, m0, m1) {
  const i0 = Math.max(0, Math.ceil(m0 / T.step)), i1 = Math.min(T.n - 1, Math.floor(m1 / T.step));
  for (let i = i0; i < i1; i++) {
    const a = T.P[i * 3 + axis] - value, b = T.P[(i + 1) * 3 + axis] - value;
    if (a === 0 || a * b < 0) return T.metre(i) + (T.metre(i + 1) - T.metre(i)) * (a === b ? 0 : a / (a - b));
  }
  return m1;
}

export default {
  id: 'otter-in-the-window-seat', name: 'Otter in the Window Seat', category: 'interior', weirdness: 0.45,
  async build(ctx) {
    await ctx.yield();                                    // the page is handed back once before any work: the parts' own loading is a step by itself
    const scene = new THREE.Scene();
    // ---- 1. the two streams of the world's own (each from a name and the seed; nothing drawn from ctx.rng here) ----
    const lookRng = ctx.core.makeRng(ctx.core.hashSeed('otter-look:' + ctx.seed));
    const castRng = ctx.core.makeRng(ctx.core.hashSeed('otter-cast:' + ctx.seed));
    const vary = ctx.vary, detail = ctx.quality.detail;
    const deal = P.dealLook(lookRng, vary.hour), LK = LOOKS[deal.name];          // the look is the stream's first draw

    // ---- 2. the route, and THE ONE TABLE OF THE ROUTE (place and tangent every 0.25 m); nothing walks the path again ----
    const path = makePath(P.ROUTE);
    await ctx.yield();
    const T = P.layTable(path), LEN = T.L, mouthM = P.mouthMetre(T);
    const tableAt = (m, out) => {                                              // a place of the route from the table
      const x = Math.min(T.n - 1.0001, Math.max(0, m / T.step)), i = Math.floor(x), f = x - i, a = i * 3, b = a + 3;
      return out.set(T.P[a] + (T.P[b] - T.P[a]) * f, T.P[a + 1] + (T.P[b + 1] - T.P[a + 1]) * f, T.P[a + 2] + (T.P[b + 2] - T.P[a + 2]) * f);
    };
    await ctx.yield();

    // ---- 3. the sky by the look; thin fog; the cloud sea under the wings; the towers, which stand still ----
    const sunV = new THREE.Vector3(deal.sun[0], deal.sun[1], deal.sun[2]).normalize();
    const sky = makeSky({ rng: ctx.rng, ...LK.sky, sunDirection: sunV });
    scene.add(sky.object);
    scene.fog = new THREE.FogExp2(sky.fogColor, LK.fog);
    await ctx.yield();
    // keep-out spheres, by place: the cabin's whole length (no puff inside the hull), the wing otter's place, and
    // the outside route's tube from behind the entry to the entered window
    const AX = P.CABIN.HULL_AXIS, keepSea = [];
    for (let i = 0; i < 7; i++) keepSea.push([AX[0], AX[1], P.CABIN.Z0 + 6.8 + i * 29, 47]);
    keepSea.push(P.OUTSIDE.WING_OTTER.KEEP.slice());
    const tube = [[-P.OUTSIDE.ENTRY_CLEAR[0] * 0.5, 40], [34, 34], [100, 30], [140, 26], [168, 24], [192, 22], [212, 20], [226, 18]], v0 = new THREE.Vector3();
    for (const [m, r] of tube) {
      if (m < 0) { keepSea.push([T.P[0] + T.T[0] * m, T.P[1] + T.T[1] * m, T.P[2] + T.T[2] * m, r]); continue; }   // behind the entry, on the entry axis
      tableAt(m, v0); keepSea.push([v0.x, v0.y, v0.z, r]);
    }
    // the sea: a puff is 66 to 180 m across and its top stands a fifth of that and the relief over `altitude`, so the
    // highest crest lies near y -33 and most near -60: under the wing roots (y -8) and the pods. No turrets (one
    // rises a whole puff over the deck, through a wing). depth 0: a sea puff's drawn depth is its own flat card's;
    // the kit's swollen depth reaches a puff's width toward the eye, and a puff under the cabin drew over its floor.
    const sea = await makeCloudFieldAsync({ rng: ctx.rng, mode: 'sea', sky, altitude: -95, relief: 30, towers: 0, depth: 0, spacing: detail < 0.7 ? 112 : 92,
      silver: LK.sea.silver, wind: [4, 0, 46], avoid: keepSea.slice(0, 16) }, ctx.yield);
    scene.add(sea.object);
    await ctx.yield();
    // the named tower (its flat top at y 21 carries the raft) and the dealt ones beyond 420 m: wind 0, the sea's own
    // noise. A kit cloud of width w reaches about 1.27 w from its middle and 1.15 x 0.72 w over its base: the named
    // one is laid 60 m wide on a base 48 m under its top, and the cabin's whole length is kept out of it by place.
    const R = P.OUTSIDE.RAFT, TW = 60, towerAt = [[R.middle[0] - 6, R.TOP_Y - 0.8 * TW, R.middle[2], TW]];
    for (const t of deal.towers) towerAt.push([t.x, t.top - 0.8 * 2 * t.r, t.z, 2 * t.r]);
    const keepTower = keepSea.slice(0, 8).map((k, i) => (i < 7 ? [k[0], k[1], k[2], 58] : k));   // the cabin's length (wider: a tower puff's swollen depth) and the wing otter
    for (const m of [140, 168, 192, 212, 226]) { tableAt(m, v0); keepTower.push([v0.x, v0.y, v0.z, 22]); }   // the flank's tube
    keepTower.push([R.middle[0], R.TOP_Y + 60, R.middle[2], 30, R.TOP_Y + 0.5, 30]);                       // the air over its flat top (an upright drum)
    const towers = await makeCloudFieldAsync({ rng: ctx.rng, mode: 'cumulus', sky, at: towerAt, height: 0.72, puffs: detail < 0.7 ? 34 : 48,
      wind: [0, 0, 0], noiseTexture: sea.noiseTexture, silver: LK.sea.silver, avoid: keepTower.slice(0, 16) }, ctx.yield);
    scene.add(towers.object);
    await ctx.yield();

    // ---- 4. the cabin's rig (the sun's direction handed ONCE: never rig.setSun later) and the light the fur reads ----
    const cabin = new THREE.Group(); cabin.name = 'cabin'; scene.add(cabin);
    const C = P.CABIN, W = D.CABIN_W;
    const rig = INT.makeLightRig({ scale: D.SCALE, sunDir: sky.sunDirection, sunColor: LK.sun, sunIntensity: LK.sunI, ambient: LK.ambient, ambientSky: LK.ambSky,
      ambientGround: LK.ambGround, bounceColor: LK.bounceColor, bounce: LK.bounce, floorY: 0, aoRadius: 0.25, dapple: { amount: 0.4, size: 0.55, speed: 1 } });
    rig.setBounds([0, 0, C.Z0], [W, D.CEIL_Y + 0.4, C.Z1], 0);
    // the windows that let light in are units -3 to 2 (blinds up); rows 3 to 8 stand in the dusk under the cove: six
    // lamps of the kit's rig along the aisle's ceiling (ctx.vary.mood warms or cools them a little). The fur reads no rig
    // lamp, so the cabin light is handed the same cove as one soft light from the ceiling, full from the first lamp's z on
    // and coming in over the three rows before it (half way to white: a brown coat under a pure blue lamp goes maroon)
    const coveCol = mixHex(LK.cove[0], LK.cove[1], vary.mood), coveZ = C.DUSK_ROW * D.PITCH - 4.2;
    const L = M.makeCabinLight(rig, { row0: C.LIGHT_ROW0, rows: C.LIGHT_ROWS, sky: LK.win[0], skyIntensity: LK.win[1], far: { sky: LK.far[0], skyIntensity: LK.far[1] },
      outside: LK.out, wind: [0, 0, 1], windGain: 1, fog: { color: sky.fogColor, density: LK.fog }, cove: { color: mixHex(coveCol, '#ffffff', 0.5), intensity: LK.cove[2] * 0.3, z: coveZ, ramp: 3 * D.PITCH },
      glowGain: DUSK.glow, glowWaitGain: DUSK.glowWait, lamps: { row0: C.DUSK_ROW }, fill: { places: [P.HERO.FILL, P.UP.FILL], from: P.HERO.FILL_FROM, color: mixHex(LK.glow[0], '#ffffff', 0.8), intensity: LK.fill } });   // fill: the hero's seat and the seat of the one stood up (places; the same at every metre)
    for (let row = C.DUSK_ROW; row <= C.ROW1; row++) rig.addLight({ position: [C.MID_X, D.CEIL_Y - 3, row * D.PITCH - 4.2], color: mixHex(coveCol, DUSK.deep, DUSK.mix), intensity: LK.cove[2] * DUSK.lamp, range: 58, flicker: 0 });
    // the gold rows' own glow: the low sun's pools on the carpet throw warm light back up the aisle (the rig's last two
    // lamps, low between rows -1 and 0 and between rows 1 and 2): seat sides, armrests and flanks beside the aisle
    // stand in a warm light of their own, unlike the violet dusk end
    for (const row of [C.ROW0 + 0.5, C.DUSK_ROW - 1.5]) rig.addLight({ position: [C.MID_X, 5, row * D.PITCH - 6], color: LK.glow[0], intensity: LK.glow[1], range: 64, flicker: 0 });
    await ctx.yield();

    // ---- 5. the seat rows of both blocks, the bay, the blinds, the partitions and their curtains ----
    // Three unit geometries serve the whole cabin (near, far, bay): each is built ONCE, resting between its pieces,
    // and shared by both blocks with one material (the far block is the same mesh mirrored by its matrix).
    const unitMat = INT.propMaterial({ rig });
    const gNear = await M.seatUnitAsync({}, ctx.yield); await ctx.yield();
    const gFar = await M.seatUnitAsync({ detail: 'far' }, ctx.yield); await ctx.yield();
    const gBay = await M.seatUnitAsync({ seats: false }, ctx.yield); await ctx.yield();
    const nearRows = [], farRows = [], blinds = [];
    for (let row = C.ROW0; row <= C.ROW1; row++) (row >= C.FAR_ROWS[0] ? farRows : nearRows).push(row);
    for (const side of [0, 1]) {
      cabin.add(M.makeSeatRows(rig, { rows: [C.BAY[0], C.BAY[1]], side, seats: false, geometry: gBay, material: unitMat }).mesh);
      cabin.add(M.makeSeatRows(rig, { rows: nearRows, side, geometry: gNear, material: unitMat }).mesh);
      cabin.add(M.makeSeatRows(rig, { rows: farRows, side, detail: 'far', geometry: gFar, material: unitMat }).mesh);
      // blinds DOWN from row 3 in both blocks (the dusk end); one half down in the sun block's row 2, beside the pair asleep
      for (let row = C.ROW0; row <= C.ROW1; row++) {
        if (row >= C.DUSK_ROW) blinds.push({ row, side, blind: 'down' });
        else if (row === C.HALF_BLIND[0] && side === C.HALF_BLIND[1]) blinds.push({ row, side, blind: 'half' });
      }
    }
    await ctx.yield();
    cabin.add(M.makeBlinds(rig, blinds, { material: unitMat }).mesh);
    await ctx.yield();
    cabin.add(M.makeBulkheads(rig, [{ z: C.Z0, face: 1 }, { z: C.Z1, face: -1 }]).mesh);
    await ctx.yield();

    // ---- 6. THE CAST from the plan's dealers: one row a seat; every seat's dice drawn before any test ----
    const cast = P.dealCast(castRng, vary, detail);
    // ---- 7. THE STATIONS by the wave's law, from the table (a number of metres flown for each seat in reach) ----
    const stations = P.layStations(T, mouthM);
    const sitters = [];                                    // { r: the plan's row, e: the entry for makeOtters, tier }
    for (const r of cast) {
      if (!r.taken) continue;
      const e = { ...P.seatAt(r.row, r.seat, r.side), mirror: r.mirror, pose: r.pose, tap: r.tap, look: r.look, look2: r.look2, nod: r.nod, phase: r.phase,
        scale: r.scale, tint: r.tint, lean: r.lean, glow: r.glow, habit: r.habit, station: P.stationFor(r, stations) };
      if (r.who === 'hero') { e.reach = P.HERO.PAW; e.reachArm = P.HERO.PAW_ARM; }   // pose 5 is one state all flight (it reads no station); glow 0: no light from a glass
      if (r.reach) { e.reach = r.reach; e.reachArm = r.reachArm; }   // the faces at the glass: a paw on the window's rim; one state all flight too
      if (r.pose === P.POSE.REST && r.who !== 'hero') { e.rise = r.rise; e.bend = r.bend; e.stand = r.stand; if (r.place) { e.position = r.place.position; e.yaw = r.place.yaw; } }   // the one stood up (plan, UP): on its hind legs on its cushion, turned to the aisle, nothing held (no reach: both paws hang before its belly); the faces at the glass, sat up and bent to their windows
      // ---- 8. the build by the chest's distance to the flown line (a thing of the place): named sitters are near ----
      let tier = 'near';
      if (r.dealt) { const c = P.ownToCabin(e, P.CHEST_OWN, r.scale); tier = P.tierOf(P.lineDist(T, c[0], c[1], c[2], P.WINDOW.WALL_M)); }
      sitters.push({ r, e, tier });
    }
    // the crew otter on its fold-down seat in the bay, facing aft, paws in its lap; it nods now and then
    const crew = { position: P.BAY.CREW.position, yaw: P.BAY.CREW.yaw, pose: P.POSE.LAP, tap: 0, look: -0.5, nod: 0.6, phase: 0.66, scale: 1, tint: [1.0, 0.98, 0.95], glow: 0, station: P.WAVE.ALWAYS };
    // ONE MORE AT THE GLASS (plan, GLASS.STAND): standing on its hind legs on a plain case in the bay at the door's own window, turned to
    // the wall, its paw on the opening's rim: from the flank outside its face shows in that window. One state all flight.
    const GS = P.GLASS.STAND, stander = { position: GS.position, yaw: GS.yaw, pose: P.POSE.REST, rise: P.UP.RISE, stand: P.UP.STAND, lean: GS.LEAN, look: GS.LOOK, look2: GS.LOOK2, nod: GS.NOD, reach: GS.PAW, reachArm: GS.PAW_ARM,
      glow: 0, phase: GS.PHASE, scale: 1, tint: [0.99, 0.97, 0.95], station: P.WAVE.NEVER };
    // the three groups outside (the OUTSIDE flag: the open sky's light, the coat streaming in the wind)
    const OUT = P.OUTSIDE;
    // THE ONE ON THE ROOF: sat up on its haunches beside the dome, its right paw on the second aerial's top; its head
    // goes by the clock between the route's start and the line abeam, and over the plan's LIFT_M metres of route it is
    // lifted and comes round with the eye (the pose's law; station and span are metres of route)
    const CR = OUT.CROWN, WO = OUT.WING_OTTER;
    const crown = { position: CR.position, yaw: CR.yaw, pose: P.POSE.REST, rise: CR.RISE, lean: CR.LEAN, look: CR.LOOK, look2: CR.LOOK2, nod: 0.3, reach: CR.PAW, reachArm: CR.PAW_ARM,
      glow: 0, outside: true, phase: CR.PHASE, station: CR.LIFT_M[0], span: CR.LIFT_M[1] - CR.LIFT_M[0] };
    // THE SLIDER: down the wing on its belly and back up it, by the world's clock (the part's SLIDE law)
    const wingOtter = { position: WO.position, yaw: WO.yaw, pose: P.POSE.BELLY, look: 0.3, slide: WO.SLIDE, bow: 0, glow: 0, outside: true, phase: WO.PHASE, station: P.WAVE.ALWAYS };
    // THE FLOATING CAST by the plan (the raft's six and the pup; the window cloud's two), the same on every visit
    const afloat = (f) => ({ ...f, pose: P.POSE.AFLOAT, glow: 0, outside: true, station: P.WAVE.ALWAYS });
    const floating = P.floatingCast(), raft = floating.map(afloat);
    if (vary.rare) { const at = { position: OUT.RARE.position, yaw: OUT.RARE.yaw, scale: 1 };            // the rare event: one more, afloat beyond the far windows
      raft.push(afloat({ ...at, tap: 0, plain: true, habit: 2, span: 0, look: P.lookAfloat(at, [D.CABIN_W, 20, OUT.RARE.position[2]]), phase: 0.17 + 5 * 0.23 })); }

    // the animal's builds, one instanced draw each; THE FIXED COAT: every build takes a generator made from the same name
    const coat = () => ctx.core.makeRng(ctx.core.hashSeed('otter-coat'));
    const lists = { near: [], mid: [], far: [], sea: [] };
    for (const s of sitters) (s.r.species === 'sea' ? lists.sea : lists[s.tier]).push(s.e);
    lists.near.push(crew, stander, crown, wingOtter); lists.sea.push(...raft);
    for (const [tier, species, list] of [['near', 'river', lists.near], ['near', 'sea', lists.sea], ['mid', 'river', lists.mid], ['far', 'river', lists.far]]) {
      if (!list.length) continue;                                             // a build nobody is dealt on this visit (the far one) is not made
      const geometry = await M.otterGeometryAsync(tier, species, ctx.yield, coat());
      await ctx.yield();
      cabin.add(M.makeOtters(L, { tier, species, list, geometry }).mesh);
      await ctx.yield();
    }

    // ---- 9. machines, screens, trays, tumblers, headphones ----
    const machines = [{ kind: 'laptop', ...P.HERO.MACHINE }], trays = [], drinks = [{ position: P.HERO.TUMBLER, phase: 0.41 }], phones = [];
    for (const { r, e } of sitters) {
      if (r.who !== 'hero' && r.machine && r.machine !== 'lap') machines.push(M.machineFor(e, r.machine, { picture: r.picture, station: e.station, seed: r.phase, back: r.back, lid: r.lid }));
      if (r.drink) drinks.push({ position: P.tumblerAt(r.row, r.seat, r.side, r.drink), phase: r.phase });
      if (r.headphones) phones.push(e);
    }
    // every seat's tray: down or stowed against the back ahead; row -1 has no back ahead, so its trays stand on a stalk
    // from the armrest (arm: true) and a stowed one is not drawn. The hero's row: seats 1 and 2 stowed, on every visit.
    for (const r of cast) { if (r.armTray && !r.trayDown) continue; const hero = r.who === 'hero'; trays.push({ row: r.row, seat: r.seat, side: r.side, down: r.trayDown, arm: r.armTray, long: hero ? P.HERO.TRAY_LONG : 0, lip: hero ? P.HERO.TRAY_LIP : 0 }); }
    const devices = await M.makeDevicesAsync(rig, machines, ctx.yield);
    cabin.add(devices.mesh);
    await ctx.yield();
    cabin.add(M.makeScreens(L, devices.screens).mesh);
    await ctx.yield();
    // THE LIGHT THAT FALLS ON THINGS (the part's makeGlow: ONE additive draw, no light of the rig): each lit screen's
    // light on the front of its own seat's back, by its screen's own station and clock; a warm pool on the tray under
    // every lit reading lamp of the dusk end (the part's lampLit: by place, the same on every visit); and the
    // ceiling's two light bars, which take the pulses' blue from update() (the same numbers as the arcs' frames)
    const glowSeats = [], pools = [];
    for (const { r, e } of sitters) if (r.who !== 'hero' && r.machine && r.machine !== 'lap' && !r.back) glowSeats.push({ row: r.row, seat: r.seat, side: r.side, station: e.station, seed: r.phase, picture: r.picture, size: (r.machine === 'laptop' ? 1 : r.machine === 'tablet' ? 0.75 : 0.5) * (r.row >= C.DUSK_ROW ? DUSK.seat : 1) });
    // (the hero's three standing arcs, always lit, throw their blue on the fronts of the seat backs of its row, the hero's own and the two empty ones: by place and their own clock)
    for (const [seat, size] of P.HERO.ARCS.LIGHT) glowSeats.push({ row: P.HERO.SEAT[0], seat, side: P.HERO.SEAT[2], station: P.WAVE.NEVER, seed: P.HERO.PHASE, picture: 0, size, open: true });
    // (a pool lies over the tray at the height of a machine's deck, so that it is seen on the keys and the deck as on the
    // tray round them; over an EMPTY seat whose lamp is lit it lies on the cushion. By the deal and the place; the same at every metre.)
    for (const t of trays) if (t.down && !t.arm && M.lampLit(t.row, t.seat, t.side, C.DUSK_ROW)) { const q = P.trayAt(t.row, t.seat, t.side); pools.push({ position: [q.position[0], D.TRAY_Y + 0.42, q.position[2]], r: 4.2, gain: DUSK.pool }); }
    for (const r of cast) if (!r.taken && r.row >= C.DUSK_ROW && M.lampLit(r.row, r.seat, r.side, C.DUSK_ROW)) { const q = P.seatAt(r.row, r.seat, r.side).position; pools.push({ position: [q[0], D.CUSHION_TOP + 0.12, q[2] - 0.9], r: 4.0, gain: DUSK.pool }); }
    const glow = M.makeGlow(L, { seats: glowSeats, pools, bars: [C.Z0, C.Z1] });
    cabin.add(glow.mesh);
    cabin.add((await M.makeTraysAsync(rig, trays, ctx.yield)).mesh);
    await ctx.yield();
    // the dress (the trolley, the crew otter's seat and the case in the bay: nothing lies on a seat's cushion and
    // nothing hangs over a cap or an armrest anywhere) is the part's, at the plan's boxes; it hands back the trolley's eight tumblers, which join
    // the sitters' drinks and the hero's in the one draw of tumblers
    const TR = P.BAY.TROLLEY;
    const dress = await M.makeDressAsync(rig, { trolley: { box: TR.BOX, cups: TR.TUMBLERS }, crew: { seat: P.BAY.CREW.SEAT_BOX, back: P.BAY.CREW.BACK_BOX }, case: { box: P.GLASS.STAND.CASE }, material: unitMat }, ctx.yield);
    cabin.add(dress.mesh);
    await ctx.yield();
    for (const t of dress.tumblers) drinks.push(t);
    cabin.add(M.makeTumblers(rig, L, drinks).object);
    cabin.add(M.makeHeadphones(L, phones).mesh);                               // the named nodder wears them on every visit
    await ctx.yield();

    // ---- 10. the outside (the outside part: hull, wings, dome, aerials, arcs, billows, wisps; each hands back
    // { object, update(dt, time, camera) } and update sets uniforms only) ----
    const E = { sunDir: sky.sunDirection, sunColor: new THREE.Color(LK.E.sun), skyColor: new THREE.Color(LK.E.sky), groundColor: new THREE.Color(LK.E.ground),
      fogColor: sky.fogColor, fogDensity: LK.fog, look: deal.name, detail, pause: ctx.yield, noise: sea.noiseTexture, rig, L, crownShade: OUT.CROWN.SHADE, crown: { position: OUT.CROWN.position, yaw: OUT.CROWN.yaw }, windowGlow: LK.glow[0] };   // crownShade, crown: the roof otter's capsules for the skin's drawn shade (it sits up) and its seat; windowGlow: the look's cabin glow, for the windows' rims
    const outside = [], take = (h) => { scene.add(h.object); outside.push(h); return h; };
    const skins = [take(await O.makeHull(E))]; await ctx.yield();
    skins.push(take(await O.makeWings(E))); await ctx.yield();
    take(O.makeDome(E)); take(O.makeAerials(E)); await ctx.yield();
    // the three kinds of arcs: standing over the dome and over the hero's lid (always lit, the same at every metre),
    // and the six frames of the two pulses, which update() works out from the path and the metres flown
    // (the dome's arcs stand in an upright plane turned between the hull's axis and the coming line, so that they show
    // wide from the route's start and from abreast alike: a thing of the place, the same at every metre)
    const HA = P.HERO.ARCS, DM = OUT.DOME;
    const standing = [
      { centre: [DM.centre[0], DM.centre[1] + DM.size[1], DM.centre[2]], normal: [0.6, 0, 0.8], up: [0, 1, 0], radii: DM.ARCS_R, fan: DM.ARCS_FAN },
      { centre: [HA.x, HA.y[0] - 0.6, HA.z], normal: [1, 0, 0], up: [0, 1, 0], radii: [2.0, 4.0, HA.y[1] - HA.y[0] + 0.6], fan: 2 * Math.asin(Math.min(1, HA.span / 2 / (HA.y[1] - HA.y[0] + 0.6))) * 180 / PI },
    ];
    const arcs = take(O.makeArcs(E, { standing, frames: 6 }));
    // the cloud tops are hollowed where the floating bodies lie (the plan's rounds, from the cast's own places)
    const WC = OUT.WINDOW_CLOUD, hollows = P.floatHollows(floating.filter((f) => !f.who.startsWith('window'))), hollowsW = P.floatHollows(floating.filter((f) => f.who.startsWith('window')));
    // the billows and the wisps share the towers' own colours (field: the kit's field round them)
    take(O.makeBillows(E, { centre: [R.middle[0], R.TOP_Y, R.middle[2]], radius: R.BILLOW_R, top: R.BILLOW_TOP, hollows, field: towers })); await ctx.yield();
    if (vary.rare) take(O.makeBillows(E, { centre: [OUT.RARE.position[0], OUT.RARE.position[1], OUT.RARE.position[2] + 3.4], radius: OUT.RARE.CLOUD_R, top: R.BILLOW_TOP, hollows: [[OUT.RARE.position[0], OUT.RARE.position[2] + 3.4, 7]], field: towers, body: true }));
    // THE WINDOW CLOUD (a place of the plan, on every visit): a small top of its own in the open sky beyond the sun
    // wing's leading edge, with a belly under it (it stands alone: body)
    take(O.makeBillows(E, { centre: WC.centre, radius: WC.R, top: WC.TOP, hollows: hollowsW, field: towers, body: true })); await ctx.yield();
    take(O.makeWisps(E, { field: towers }));
    await ctx.yield();

    // THE SLIDER'S DRAWN SHADE goes with it: the two skins' last three capsules are the wing otter's (the outside part
    // lays them from the plan's WING_OTTER.SHADE at the top of the slide); update() moves them by the part's own slide
    // law through the skins' setShade (uniforms only).
    const shadeOwn = WO.SHADE.map((c) => [[c[0], c[1], c[2]], [c[3], c[4], c[5]], c[6]]);
    const shadeAt = (q, sl, out) => { const c1 = Math.cos(sl[1]), s1 = Math.sin(sl[1]), c2 = Math.cos(WO.yaw), s2 = Math.sin(WO.yaw), z0 = q[2] - M.SLIDE.PIVOT;
      const x1 = q[0] * c1 + z0 * s1, z1 = z0 * c1 - q[0] * s1 + M.SLIDE.PIVOT;
      return out.set(WO.position[0] + x1 * c2 + z1 * s2 + WO.SLIDE[0] * sl[0], WO.position[1] + q[1] + WO.SLIDE[1] * sl[0], WO.position[2] + z1 * c2 - x1 * s2 + WO.SLIDE[2] * sl[0]); };
    const sv = new THREE.Vector3(), sw2 = new THREE.Vector3();

    // ---- 11. window light: shafts with thickness from the windows of units -3 to 2 (they lie across the flown line
    // in the bay and the aisle of the gold rows; each begins 11.4 m in from its window: below), and a few dim motes ----
    const light = INT.makeWindowLight({ rig, rng: ctx.rng.fork('window-light'), panes: false, shafts: true, motes: true, shaftGain: LK.shaftGain * 1.25, shaftDensity: 0.24,
      motesPerWindow: Math.round(40 * detail), maxMotes: 400, moteSize: 0.0026, moteGain: 0.3 });
    // THE HERO'S OWN WINDOW THROWS NO SHAFT (a thing of the place, made once here): its beam lay between the eye and the
    // hero for the whole last leg and washed the animal to one pale gold shape. The sun still falls through that window
    // on its fur, its seat and its machine, and the other five windows keep their shafts. (A shaft row is one box of
    // twelve triangles a window, in the windows' order: the hero's box is taken out of the row's index.)
    for (const s of light.shafts) { const g = s.mesh.children[0].geometry, ix = Array.from(g.index.array); ix.splice((P.HERO.SEAT[0] - C.LIGHT_ROW0) * 36, 36); g.setIndex(ix); }
    // THE SHAFTS BEGIN BEYOND THE WINDOW SEATS (a thing of the place, made once here; the lead's ruling E8). A shaft is a
    // box of haze drawn over whatever stands inside it, the haze behind a body counted with the haze before it: an otter
    // sat or stood AT the glass (the two faces at the glass in rows 1 and 2, the one stood at the bay's window, the
    // front row's window seat) stood in the root of its own window's beam and, seen from the aisle toward the low sun,
    // was washed to one pale gold shape, near white (two strangers of the second bar: "blown-out", "glowing as if lit
    // wrongly"). Every box of the row and the row's own origin (which its shader measures the box from) are moved along
    // the sun's ray until they begin SHAFT_X metres in from the wall: the beams still lie across the middle seats, the
    // aisle and the bay, their haze comes in softly there by the kit's own law, and the first 11.4 m from the glass are
    // clear air. The sun and the windows' sky fall on fur and seats as before; nothing here reads the lens or a seed.
    { const d = rig.uniforms.uSunDir.value, k = -SHAFT_X / Math.max(-d.x, 0.05);
      for (const s of light.shafts) { const m = s.mesh.children[0]; m.geometry.translate(d.x * k, d.y * k, d.z * k); m.material.uniforms.uO.value.addScaledVector(d, k); } }
    cabin.add(light.object);
    await ctx.yield();

    // ---- 12. THE LOOKS, by PLACE: each opens and closes where the eye comes level with a named place, found in the
    // table and turned into u here; each aim is a named thing. Where the design says two overlap, they overlap. ----
    const lev = (axis, value, m0, m1) => levelMetre(T, axis, value, m0, m1);
    const mRoof = lev(0, -12, 0, P.WINDOW.SKIN_M), mSkin = P.WINDOW.SKIN_M, mWall = P.WINDOW.WALL_M, mWheel = P.ROUTE_LAW.WHEEL_M;
    const mAbeamRaft = lev(2, R.middle[2], mRoof, mSkin), mZ68 = lev(2, -68, mRoof, mSkin), mRaftGo = lev(2, R.middle[2] + 21, mRoof, mSkin);
    const u = (m) => m / LEN, aimAhead = new THREE.Vector3(), aimAisle = new THREE.Vector3(), aimFlank = new THREE.Vector3(), aimRow = new THREE.Vector3(), FLANK_RUN = 1.0, FLANK_DROP = 4, FLANK_Z = [C.Z0 - D.PITCH, C.Z0], FLANK_NEAR = [4, 16], AISLE_OFF = [70, 15], AISLE_Y = 18, LAP_Y = 17, UP_Y = 23.5, UP_OFF = 2.5, AISLE_SWING = [45, 62];
    const typist = cast.find((r) => r.who === 'typist'), tp = P.seatAt(typist.row, typist.seat, typist.side).position;
    const faceOf = (row, side, dy) => { const h = P.ownToCabin(P.seatAt(row, 2, side), P.HEAD_OWN, 1); return [h[0], h[1] + dy, h[2] - 0.6]; };
    const aimWheel = new THREE.Vector3(...faceOf(C.FAR_ROWS[0], 1, -0.7));
    // the laps of the sun block's aisle seats in rows 1 to 4 (2.4 m before the seat's own place, y 17), and where the
    // long look's aim goes over to each: while the eye is 12 to 4 m before the line of the row in front of it
    const laps = [];
    for (let row = 1; row < C.FAR_ROWS[0]; row++) { const sp = P.seatAt(row, 2, 0).position, back = (row - 1) * D.PITCH; laps.push({ at: new THREE.Vector3(sp[0], LAP_Y, sp[2] - 2.4), from: back - 12, to: back - 4 }); }
    // row 1's is THE ONE STOOD UP (plan, UP: the middle seat, where it stands on its cushion: upAt): the aim rests
    // beside its HEAD on the aisle's side (UP_Y 23.5; it was its chest, 20.5), 1.5 m before the place it stands: the
    // one stood up and the face at the glass beyond it fill the picture; the aisle seat of that row, right under the
    // eye there, is kept empty by the plan (the one in headphones who sat in it was a head cut by the picture's lower edge)
    { const up = P.upAt().position; laps[0].at.set(up[0] + UP_OFF, UP_Y, up[2] - 1.5); }
    const aimDusk = new THREE.Vector3(C.MID_X, 19, (C.FAR_ROWS[0] + 1.5) * D.PITCH);   // the aisle's middle between rows 6 and 7, at head height
    const CROWN_AIM_DROP = 3;
    const pois = [
      // the crown otter (the aim: its chest, 3 m under its head, so that the animal stands whole in the picture for
      // as long as its size there lets it), from the route's start until the eye is 5 m short of being level with it: THE
      // LOOK LETS GO OF IT BEFORE THE EYE IS ABOVE IT. Its weight falls over the last stretch before that, while the
      // animal, sat up beside the dome, is still seen from its front and side
      { at: [OUT.CROWN.HEAD[0], OUT.CROWN.HEAD[1] - CROWN_AIM_DROP, OUT.CROWN.HEAD[2]], from: 0, to: u(lev(0, OUT.CROWN.HEAD[0] + 5, 0, mRoof)), weight: 0.7, fade: 0.35 },
      // then THE DOME UNDER ITS THREE ARCS (its crown, a metre over it), from the eye level with x 72 to x 30: the gaze
      // stays down on the roof and turns up to 30 degrees toward the dome, so that the animal, 8 m beside the line and
      // seen from its side with its face, leaves by the frame's SIDE while the gaze is still down beside it (not by a
      // corner under a gaze gone back to the sky); the dome and its arcs stand in the right of the picture, the
      // raft and the cloud sea in the left, and the gaze comes back to the way flown as the dome falls behind
      { at: [DM.centre[0], DM.centre[1] + DM.size[1] + 1, DM.centre[2]], from: u(lev(0, 72, 0, mRoof)), to: u(lev(0, 30, 0, mRoof)), weight: 0.55, fade: 0.5 },
      // THE RAFT IS HELD INSIDE THE FRAME WHILE IT IS NEAR: its middle, strongly, from the eye level with x 10 on the
      // roof until the eye has come down past it (level with a place 21 m beyond the raft's middle). The look's weight
      // is whole until the eye is nearly abeam of the raft and then goes over evenly to the look below, the way the line
      // itself turns: the raft leaves by the frame's side in one turn and is not left hanging in a corner
      { at: R.middle, from: u(lev(0, 10, 0, mRoof)), to: u(mRaftGo), weight: 0.9, fade: 0.36 },
      // ONE LOOK FROM THE RAFT TO THE ENTERED WINDOW, its aim a law of the eye's own place (it slides with the metres
      // flown). First the slider's way on the wing (the middle of it): the wing, its otter and, while the eye is
      // still high, the cloud of two in the sky beyond the wing's leading edge; the hull's windows on the left. Then, while the eye comes from one seat pitch before the bay's front
      // partition to level with that partition (FLANK_Z: two places of the cabin), the aim goes over
      // to THE ROW OF WINDOWS: the point of the row at the skin (FLANK_DROP under the windows' middles, so that the
      // wing and the cloud sea stay in the frame under them) that lies FLANK_RUN metres further up the cabin than
      // the entered window for every metre the eye still stands off the skin. The row is seen about 40 degrees off
      // square, the entered window on the left and growing, the windows beyond it running away to the right; within
      // FLANK_NEAR metres of the skin the aim runs down the row to the entered window itself, and the look closes
      // 6 m off the skin (the eye level with x -6), over the opening of the look through the window at the typist.
      // It opens 10 m of flight before the eye is abeam of the raft and comes on over a quarter of its length, so
      // that the turn from the raft to the wing is spread over about 18 m flown (the film's fastest turn there is
      // about 50 degrees a second; opened abeam and shorter it was 63)
      { at: (time, uu) => { tableAt(uu * LEN, aimFlank); const off = Math.max(0, P.WINDOW.X[0] - aimFlank.x), ss = THREE.MathUtils.smoothstep, k = ss(aimFlank.z, FLANK_Z[0], FLANK_Z[1]);
        aimRow.set(P.WINDOW.X[0], P.WINDOW.Y - FLANK_DROP, P.WINDOW.Z + FLANK_RUN * off * ss(off, FLANK_NEAR[0], FLANK_NEAR[1]));
        return aimFlank.set(WO.HEAD[0], WO.HEAD[1], WO.HEAD[2]).lerp(aimRow, k); },
        from: u(mAbeamRaft - 10), to: u(lev(0, -6, mZ68, mSkin)), weight: 0.85, fade: 0.24 },
      // the typist's paws on its keys, from 12 m outside the skin (the eye level with x -12 on the way in) until it is abeam
      { at: [tp[0], 14.6, tp[2] - 4.9], from: u(lev(0, -12, mZ68, mSkin)), to: u(lev(2, tp[2] - 5, mWall, mWheel[0])), weight: 0.7 },
      // ONE LOOK FROM THE BAY TO THE WHEEL, its aim a law of the eye's own place (it slides with the metres flown).
      // The typist, the empty seat beside the one stood up, the pair asleep, the phone held the wrong way round and
      // row 4's sitter all lie on one line (the sun block's aisle seats, x 26.4), and the line flown climbs beside them to a gallery.
      // - In the bay the aim is the point of that line 70 degrees off the way flown, at y 18 (between a sitter's paws
      //   and its face): the typist's head, which leans 3 m forward of its seat, comes through the middle large.
      // - From the eye 11 m before the typist's seat to 1 m past it the aim runs out along the line to 15 degrees off
      //   the way flown: the eye crosses the first row's backs looking up the whole cabin (the caps, the lit aisle,
      //   the coves, the blue end, the arcs opening ahead), not across at the side of a seat's back.
      // - Then the aim rests on a lap in turn (rows 1 to 4), going over to each while the eye is 12 to 4 m before the
      //   line of the row in front of it: by then the eye is above the caps and the sitter shows whole over them.
      // - Where the wheel begins (the eye level with z 45 to z 62) the aim leaves the line for THE FACE OF ROW 5'S
      //   SITTER ON THE FAR BLOCK'S AISLE SEAT, the way the wheel turns, and rests on it (its two neighbours beside
      //   it) until the eye is level with x 38 on the wheel. It crosses the aisle by way of the aisle's middle far
      //   down the dusk rows (one curve through three points): the crossing lifts the gaze down the length of the
      //   dusk and does not drag it across the carpet.
      // The aisle seats of rows -1 to 5 are never empty, but those of rows 0 and 1 (the plan's rule NO_EMPTY_AISLE and NAMED). The look opens in the bay
      // (the eye level with z -47, before the typist's look lets go). The hero's row is not looked into from the
      // aisle: it is the last leg's own (a glance across its two empty seats put the side of a seat's back in the
      // middle of the picture for 7 m). By the engine's gaze law in node the gaze turns at 45 degrees a second at
      // the most in the bay, 40 past the first rows and 42 from the gallery to the wheel's end.
      { at: (time, uu) => { tableAt(uu * LEN, aimAisle); const z = aimAisle.z, ss = THREE.MathUtils.smoothstep;
        const off = (AISLE_OFF[0] + (AISLE_OFF[1] - AISLE_OFF[0]) * ss(z, tp[2] - 11, tp[2] + 1)) * Math.PI / 180;
        aimAisle.set(tp[0], AISLE_Y, z + (aimAisle.x - tp[0]) / Math.tan(off));
        for (const lap of laps) aimAisle.lerp(lap.at, ss(z, lap.from, lap.to));
        const sw = ss(z, AISLE_SWING[0], AISLE_SWING[1]);
        return aimAisle.multiplyScalar((1 - sw) * (1 - sw)).addScaledVector(aimDusk, 2 * sw * (1 - sw)).addScaledVector(aimWheel, sw * sw); },
        from: u(lev(2, -47, mWall, mWheel[0])), to: u(lev(0, 38, mWheel[0], mWheel[1])), weight: 0.8, fade: 0.12 },
      // the machines ahead on the far block: 22 m ahead of the eye's own place on the route, at tray height, 4 m
      // outboard of the line and never inboard of x 56; it slides with the metres flown
      { at: (time, uu) => { tableAt(Math.min(LEN, uu * LEN + 22), aimAhead); aimAhead.x = Math.max(56, aimAhead.x + 4); aimAhead.y = 15; return aimAhead; },
        from: u(lev(0, 30, mWheel[0], mWheel[1])), to: u(lev(2, 5, mWheel[1], mouthM)), weight: 0.6, fade: 0.2 },
      // the hero: a point 3 m over the middle between its head and its glass (y 20.8; it was 17.8: the sitters right
      // under the eye on the swing out fall below the picture, and the hero's three arcs stand whole in it); held until
      // the engine lets every look go on the last heading.
      // It opens where the eye is level with z 24, over the far block's row 2: the swing out then looks across the cabin
      // at the gold side and the hero's row, not level at the front partition.
      { at: [5.4, 20.8, -8.5], from: u(lev(2, 24, mWheel[1], mouthM)), to: 1, weight: 0.7, fade: 0.15 },
    ];

    // ---- 14. the sky's own shader is compiled last ----
    await sky.prewarm(ctx.renderer, null, scene);
    const fv = new THREE.Vector3(), ft = new THREE.Vector3(1, 0, 0), A = P.ARCS;
    return {
      scene, path, duration: P.FLIGHT.DURATION, pace: (uu) => P.paceOf(uu * LEN),
      camera: { ...P.CAMERA }, pois,
      // ---- 13. the way out: the engine's own opening in the frame of the hero's turned laptop (a bare rectangle, the
      // ring look named so that none is dealt, a lit waiting glass of the waiting screens' own blue until the next world shows) ----
      portal: { ...P.PORTAL },
      post: LK.post,
      style: 'none', ride: 'none', companion: 'none',
      update(dt, time, camera, uu) {
        const d = uu * LEN;                                              // the metres flown: the one key of every scripted thing
        sky.update(dt, time, camera); sea.update(dt, time, camera); towers.update(dt, time, camera);
        rig.update(time, cabin); L.update(time, camera, ctx.renderer);
        L.setSignal(d, P.WAVE.RAMP);                                              // the wave, and the crown otter's lift of its head
        light.update(dt, time, camera);
        {
          // the two pulses that can live at d, three arcs each: place and tangent from the path at each arc's route
          // metre, the radius by the plan's law, the strength with the coming-in, the going-out (by its life, and by
          // its station's metres to the mouth of the hero's row gap) and the hurry guard
          const hurry = P.hurryGuard(ctx.flight.rate), k1 = Math.floor(d / A.GAP);
          for (let q = 0; q < 2; q++) {
            const k = k1 - 1 + q, born = A.GAP * k, l = d - born, station = born + A.RUN * l;
            const live = k >= 0 && born <= mouthM - A.NO_BIRTH && l >= 0 && l <= A.LIFE && station <= mouthM;
            const lin = Math.min(1, Math.max(0, l / A.IN)), lout = Math.min(1, Math.max(0, (A.LIFE - l) / A.OUT));
            const lm = Math.min(1, Math.max(0, (mouthM - station) / A.MOUTH_EASE));     // out by the station's own metres to the mouth (the plan's pulseAt)
            const strength = live ? lin * lin * (3 - 2 * lin) * lout * lout * (3 - 2 * lout) * lm * lm * (3 - 2 * lm) * hurry : 0;
            if (live) { path.posAtDist(station, fv); path.tangentAtDist(station, ft); glow.setPulse(q, fv.z, ft.z, strength); } else glow.setPulse(q, 0, 0, 0);   // the ceiling's blue: where this pulse stands
            for (let j = 0; j < A.N; j++) {
              const s = station - j * A.APART, on = live && s >= born;
              if (on) { path.posAtDist(s, fv); path.tangentAtDist(s, ft); }
              arcs.setFrame(q * 3 + j, fv.x, fv.y, fv.z, ft.x, ft.y, ft.z, on ? P.arcRadius(j, s, l) : 1, on ? strength : 0);
            }
          }
        }
        for (let i = 0; i < outside.length; i++) outside[i].update(dt, time, camera);
        { const sl = M.slideAt(time, WO.PHASE);                                    // the slider's shade, by the same clock and law as its body
          for (let k = 0; k < shadeOwn.length; k++) { const c = shadeOwn[k]; shadeAt(c[0], sl, sv); shadeAt(c[1], sl, sw2); for (const h of skins) h.setShade(k, sv, sw2, c[2]); } }
      },
      dispose() {},
    };
  },
};
